{# ── 1. Model tiers (rows in _data/aiStack.yaml) ── #}
<section class="not-prose mb-12" aria-labelledby="tiers-heading">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
    <h2 id="tiers-heading" class="editorial-title">Model Tiers</h2>
    <span class="meta-line">{{ aiStack.monthly }}</span>
  </div>
  <p class="editorial-support-compact mb-3">Three tiers by cost. A frontier model plans and reviews, cheap hosted models do the building, and a local model catches whatever falls through.</p>

  <div class="surface overflow-hidden">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-xs md:text-sm font-sans">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-stone-100/60 dark:bg-stone-900/60 font-mono text-[0.78rem] uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Tier</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Service</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Cost</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Role</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Models</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Harness</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-800">
          {% for row in aiStack.tiers | enabled %}
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 font-mono whitespace-nowrap"><strong>{{ row.tier }}</strong> <span class="meta-text">{{ row.label }}</span></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 font-mono font-semibold">{% if row.href %}<a href="{{ row.href }}" class="accent-link">{{ row.service }}</a>{% else %}{{ row.service }}{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 meta-text">{{ row.cost }}</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 editorial-support-compact">{{ row.role }}</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 font-mono text-[0.8rem]">
              {% for m in row.models %}{% if loop.first %}<strong>{{ m.name }}</strong>{% else %}, {{ m.name }}{% endif %}{% if m.rank %} <span class="meta-text">({{ m.rank }})</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
            </td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 meta-text">{{ row.harness }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ── 2. Team workflow ── #}
<section class="not-prose mb-12" aria-labelledby="herding-heading">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
    <h2 id="herding-heading" class="editorial-title">Team Workflow</h2>
    <span class="meta-line">Experimenting</span>
  </div>
  <div class="surface surface-padding">
    <p class="editorial-support-compact m-0">
      I'm trying out Herding for team-based work. Opus runs as the supervisor in one pane: it breaks a goal into bounded tasks on a shared board and assigns them to worker panes, each in its own git worktree. DeepSeek through Vibe takes the build tasks, ZCode workers take the grunt work, and pi on the local model picks up anything left when the hosted quotas run dry. Opus reviews the findings and diffs before anything merges.
    </p>
    <p class="editorial-support-compact mt-3 mb-0">
      The <a href="https://opencode.ai" class="accent-link">OpenCode</a> team is <a href="https://x.com/thdxr/status/2118755687274532893" class="accent-link">trying the same split</a>, per Dax Raad: every subagent on DeepSeek Flash, and Opus 5.5 only on the primary. His notes so far are to be strict about scope when creating a task, to "ask for proof of work instead of a summary", and to do a one-step review of the diff "to make sure it's not totally off".
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ── 3. Hermes agents (rows in _data/aiStack.yaml) ── #}
<section class="not-prose mb-12" aria-labelledby="hermes-heading">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
    <h2 id="hermes-heading" class="editorial-title">Hermes Agents</h2>
    <span class="meta-line">{{ aiStack.hermes | enabled | length }} machines</span>
  </div>
  <p class="editorial-support-compact mb-3">Two always-on Hermes agents, one for life admin and one for the lab. Each runs on a cheap default and falls back down the chain in order when a provider fails or runs out.</p>

  <div class="surface overflow-hidden">
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-xs md:text-sm font-sans">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-stone-100/60 dark:bg-stone-900/60 font-mono text-[0.78rem] uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Host</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Work</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Primary</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-3 md:px-4 font-semibold">Fallbacks, in order</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-800">
          {% for agent in aiStack.hermes | enabled %}
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 font-mono font-semibold">{{ agent.host }}</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 meta-text">{{ agent.work }}</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 font-mono text-[0.8rem]"><strong>{{ agent.primary }}</strong></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-3 md:px-4 font-mono text-[0.8rem]">{% for f in agent.fallbacks %}{{ loop.index }}. {{ f }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ── 4. Nested Prompts & Skills ── #}
<section class="not-prose mb-12" aria-label="Prompts and Skills">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">

    {# Evaluation Prompts (/ai/prompts/) #}
    <div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
        <h2 class="editorial-title">Prompts</h2>
        <a href="/ai/prompts/" class="home-panel-link">All {{ collections.prompts | length }} prompts →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="surface divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-800">
        {% for prompt in collections.prompts | reverse | head(5) %}
          <article class="p-3.5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
              <a href="{{ prompt.url }}" class="editorial-title-link-compact title-hover no-underline">{{ prompt.data.title }}</a>
              {% if prompt.data.category %}<span class="badge badge-tag badge-compact shrink-0">{{ prompt.data.category }}</span>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {% if prompt.data.description %}
              <p class="editorial-support-compact mt-1 m-0 line-clamp-2">{{ prompt.data.description }}</p>
            {% endif %}
          </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Agent Skills (/ai/skills/) #}
    <div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
        <h2 class="editorial-title">Skills</h2>
        <a href="/ai/skills/" class="home-panel-link">Skills page →</a>
      </div>
      {% if collections.agentSkills | length %}
        <div class="surface divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-800">
          {% for skill in collections.agentSkills | reverse | head(5) %}
            <article class="p-3.5">
              <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                <a href="{{ skill.url }}" class="editorial-title-link-compact title-hover no-underline">{{ skill.data.title }}</a>
                {% if skill.data.sourceName %}<span class="meta-text shrink-0">{{ skill.data.sourceName }}</span>{% endif %}
              </div>
              {% if skill.data.description %}
                <p class="editorial-support-compact mt-1 m-0 line-clamp-2">{{ skill.data.description }}</p>
              {% endif %}
            </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      {% else %}
        <div class="surface surface-padding">
          <p class="editorial-support-compact m-0">
            Reusable <code>SKILL.md</code> instruction files I write and use for agent workflows, voice calibration, and local GPU handoffs. Browse published skills on <a href="/ai/skills/" class="accent-link">/ai/skills/</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
